{#-
  Document skeleton: the Science Europe DMP questions mapped onto the Norwegian
  knowledge model (research.data.no:norway-generic).

  Sections and the 15 numbered questions follow the Science Europe "Practical Guide
  to the International Alignment of Research Data Management"; headings are numbered
  <section><letter> (1a, 1b, 2a, ...) exactly as the guide numbers them. Each block lists
  anchor questions as "<chapterKey>.<questionKey>" json.key pairs; keys are
  chapter-qualified because json.key is only unique within a chapter. Every anchor
  is a top-level question of a live (annotated) chapter, so its reply path is
  deterministic; follow-up questions and list items below an anchor are rendered
  recursively and must not be listed here.

  Anchors are rendered at most once per document (see renderByKey in
  _renderers.html.j2), so the first block listing a key wins.

  Selection is driven by the KM's "RCN/Science Europe" tag. Anchors that do not
  carry that tag but that a Science Europe question explicitly asks for are included
  anyway; tools/check_sections.py reports both directions of that comparison.

  Question 5d (persistent identifiers) has no anchor of its own: the Norwegian model
  asks about PIDs inside the dataset and software list questions, which are rendered
  under questions 5a and 5c. A block with no resolvable anchor renders nothing at
  all, heading included (see content.html.j2).

  Questions used for the front matter (contributors, project metadata, DMP title,
  related DMPs) are handled in header.html.j2 / contributors.html.j2 /
  projects.html.j2 and are absent here.
-#}
{%- set sections = [
  {
    "id": "sec-data-collection",
    "title": "Section 1: Data description and collection or re-use of existing data",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "heading": "1a. How will new data be collected or produced and/or how will existing data be re-used?",
        "anchors": [
          "reusingCollectingChapter.hasMeasuredData",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.hasNonMeasuredData",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.collectsPhysicalSample",
          "reusingCollectingChapter.reDatasetsRecords",
